#!/bin/sh
# Managed by ansible - roles/fuel_signal
# Pulls the checkout to latest (today's snapshot CSV, committed by
# upstream's own daily-snapshot GitHub Action, arrives this way - see
# README's "Daily update" section), syncs dependencies, then mirrors
# upstream's own "Daily DB update" GitHub Actions workflow: load the new
# snapshot, forward-fill daily_prices, then re-classify stations and
# re-score LGA leadership for *today only* (both default to a single-date
# run - see fuel_signal.classify/lga_leadership --help - not the
# --start-date backfill mode used for a from-scratch rebuild). All output
# lands in the journal via this unit's stdout/stderr.
#
# fill alone isn't enough for the always-on workbench: /classification-health
# reads station_class/classification_summary and /lead-lag reads
# lga_leadership, neither of which fill touches - only classify/
# lga_leadership populate those. No fuel_signal.signal call - the buy/wait
# CLI signal isn't needed here.
#
# --snapshot-date is passed explicitly (UTC, computed here) rather than
# left to classify/lga_leadership's own `date.today()` default, which
# reads the host's local date - same reasoning fuel_signal_daily_update_
# oncalendar is explicit UTC rather than relying on viking's system
# timezone.
#
# This is a deliberate exception to "the ansible role never runs git pull"
# (see fuelsignal-deploy.sh.j2): that invariant is about the *ansible role*
# not silently redeploying code as a side effect of an unrelated playbook
# run, not about all automation on the box. This timer intentionally keeps
# the checkout bleeding-edge daily. It does NOT restart
# fuelsignal-workbench.service though - the running Flask process doesn't
# reload code from disk anyway, and it queries SQLite fresh per request
# rather than caching this data at startup, so no restart is needed for
# new data to show up - only fuelsignal-deploy's explicit restart puts new
# *code* in front of users.
set -eu
cd "{{ fuel_signal_repo_dir }}"
git pull --ff-only
/usr/local/bin/uv sync

today="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)"
/usr/local/bin/uv run python -m fuel_signal.db
/usr/local/bin/uv run python -m fuel_signal.fill
/usr/local/bin/uv run python -m fuel_signal.classify --snapshot-date "$today"
/usr/local/bin/uv run python -m fuel_signal.lga_leadership --snapshot-date "$today"
